# No em dashes or en dashes

Do not use em dashes (`—`, U+2014) or en dashes (`–`, U+2013) anywhere in the codebase: user-facing copy, comments, JSDoc, markdown, or plan text.

## Use instead

- A normal hyphen with spaces: ` - ` (e.g. `This fits - continue`)
- For numeric ranges: a hyphen with no spaces (e.g. `0-3`, not `0–3`)
- Or rephrase with a colon, comma, or period when clearer

```tsx
// BAD
'This fits — continue'
/** Map capability to 0–2 */

// GOOD
'This fits - continue'
/** Map capability to 0-2 */
```

When editing existing text that contains `—` or `–`, replace it with `-` in the same pass.
